WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.010
Uganda: landlocked, on the equator,
and home to 45.9 million people.

2
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:10.850
In 2006, oil was discovered
near Lake Albert.

3
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:15.570
An export pipeline runs 1,443 kilometres,

4
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:18.870
from Hoima to the port
of Tanga, in Tanzania.

5
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:23.990
Net aid in 2023: 2.26 billion dollars.

6
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:28.490
Foreign direct investment
in 2024: 3.12 billion.

7
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:33.870
So Uganda now gets more from
foreign investors than from aid.

8
00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.010
Is that good for its development?

9
00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:40.470
In this mission, you'll sort aid
by who gives it and on what terms.

10
00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:43.530
Then you'll follow oil,
trade and remittances,

11
00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:46.150
and weigh what each brings Uganda.

12
00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:51.640
Your mission: decide whether more investment
than aid is good for Uganda's development.
